Psalm 119:73-80

73 It was your hánds that máde me and sháped me;
gránt me ínsight to léarn your commánds.
74 Thóse who revére you sée me and rejóice,
for I trúst in your wórd.

75 O LÓRD, I knów that your decrées are ríght;
though I am húmbled, yóu are júst.
76 Let your mérciful lóve consóle me
by your prómise to your sérvant.

77 Shów me compássion, that I may líve,
for your láw is my delíght.
78 Let the árrogant be shámed who defléct me with líes;
as for mé, I will pónder your précepts.

79 Let thóse who féar you túrn to me,
that they may knów your decrées.
80  Let my héart be blámeless in your státutes,
that I may not be pút to sháme.

Glóry to the Fáther, and to the Són,
and to the Hóly Spírit:
as it wás in the begínning, is nów,
and will be for éver. Amén.
